commit 9d6069d9b5eba7cd658c52e6f45035d2c64b5072

C03: the image-scope statement of a screen reading is not an asserted failure (SCREEN1419)

SCREEN1417 measured the screen-content questions and describe forms: capture and read completed and verified, and the honest preface («no puedo describir imágenes, sólo leer el texto de la pantalla») was vetoed by the composer's failure lens as asserted_failure on a successful mission; the App's ReversesSuccessfulResult ends in the same LooksLikeFailure test and would have vetoed it too.

llm.compose_visible_defect: for a verified screen reading (single operation or mission step), the clause that says images cannot be described is masked from the failure lens before the asserted-failure check; every other failure claim is still vetoed.
Baxy.App.UserMessagePolicy.ReversesSuccessfulResult: the same clause is masked through WithoutScreenReadingImageScope when the source carries a verified ocr.read (top level or among the mission steps), as the empty known-file finding already is.

App recompiled (BUILD1419). Offline probe: the prefaced reading passes the mind's lens, a real failure claim is still asserted_failure. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


